# Normalise line endings to LF in the repository and on checkout, everywhere.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone with the default core.autocrlf=true writes CRLF
# to disk, and `prettier --check` — which expects LF — fails on every file. The
# gate has to give the same answer on every machine, so the working copy is
# pinned rather than each developer's git config.
* text=auto eol=lf
